"""Integrated Execution Terminal & Application Console for CyberSecuritySuite.

SECURITY & EXECUTION ARCHITECTURE:
-----------------------------------
1. Interactive Command Console:
   - This terminal functions as an UNRESTRICTED OPERATOR CONSOLE. It allows security
     engineers and penetration testers to execute standard bash/system commands (e.g. ls,
     cd, python scripts, diagnostics, and customized security tooling).
   - Session Tracking: When an active project is selected, interactive terminal sessions,
     commands, and outputs are automatically audited, recorded into SQLite, scrubbed of
     sensitive credentials via regex redaction, and hashed in the Evidence Vault (SHA-256).
   - The interactive shell is intentionally unrestricted to avoid impeding authorized manual
     penetration testing operations.

2. Automated Assessment Adapters vs. Terminal:
   - In contrast to the interactive operator terminal, all AUTOMATED ASSESSMENT ADAPTERS
     (NmapAdapter, NiktoAdapter, SQLMapAdapter, HydraAdapter, WAFW00FAdapter, GobusterAdapter)
     are strictly SCOPE-ENFORCED through ToolExecutionService and ScopeAuthorizationService.
   - Automated adapters unconditionally fail-closed before subprocess creation if a target
     is not authorized within the active project scope.
   - High-risk operations (intrusive SQLMap injection tests or intensive Hydra brute-force)
     require explicit operator confirmation guards (confirmed_high_risk=True).

Provides:
1. Interactive Command Shell with line input, command history, working directory
   tracking, cancellation, and real-time streaming output.
2. Application & Tool Log Console for background scanners and framework events.
"""

